            <ArticleTitle>[A woman with urinary tract infections and flank pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A3865</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 52-year-old woman presented with recurrent urinary tract infections and flank pain. Both an abdominal CT-scan and a plain abdominal X-ray showed bilateral nephrocalcinosis and a kidney stone in the left ureter. These findings are suggestive of medullary sponge kidneys.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
